<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore shares face profit taking, undertone firm.</title>
<headline>Singapore shares face profit taking, undertone firm.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore shares are expected to come under some profit taking on Thursday but the undertone should remain firm.</p>
<p>&quot;There could be some profit taking after the strong gains yesterday. But sentiment remains quite upbeat,&quot; said a broker with a Singapore firm.</p>
<p>The Straits Times Industrials Index closed 24.18 points higher at 1,974.69 on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--Doreen Siow, Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
